<article class="env-proposition" id="03PJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03PJ">Proposition <span data-tag="03PJ">59.27.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and $\mathcal{F}$ an abelian sheaf on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{\acute{e}tale}$. Then $\mathcal{F}|_{S_{\acute{e}tale}}$ is a sheaf on $S_{\acute{e}tale}$ and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ p_{\acute{e}tale}(S, \mathcal{F}|_{S_{\acute{e}tale}}) = H^ p_{\acute{e}tale}(S, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $p \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/03YX" data-tag="03YX">59.20.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>